{
  "propositions": [
    {
      "text": "IPCC第六次评估报告（AR6）综合报告：决策者摘要已发布。",
      "exactQuote": "IPCC Sixth Assessment Report (AR6) Synthesis Report: Summary for Policymakers",
      "blockId": "c-climate-001#block-0"
    },
    {
      "text": "内容来源于IPCC官方网站。",
      "exactQuote": "Content sourced from official IPCC website (https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/syr/) and headline statements page. Full report publicly available.",
      "blockId": "c-climate-001#block-2"
    },
    {
      "text": "该报告于2023年3月19日发布。",
      "exactQuote": "Published: 19 March 2023 (approved at IPCC 58th Session, Interlaken, Switzerland)",
      "blockId": "c-climate-001#block-3"
    },
    {
      "text": "核心撰写团队包括Hoesung Lee（主席）、Katherine Calvin、Dipak Dasgupta等人。",
      "exactQuote": "Core Writing Team: Hoesung Lee (Chair), Katherine Calvin, Dipak Dasgupta, et al.",
      "blockId": "c-climate-001#block-3"
    },
    {
      "text": "该报告的DOI为10.59327/IPCC/AR6-9789291691647。",
      "exactQuote": "DOI: 10.59327/IPCC/AR6-9789291691647",
      "blockId": "c-climate-001#block-3"
    },
    {
      "text": "人类活动，主要通过温室气体排放，已经明确导致了全球变暖。",
      "exactQuote": "Human activities, principally through emissions of greenhouse gases, have unequivocally caused global warming",
      "blockId": "c-climate-001#block-5"
    },
    {
      "text": "2011-2020年全球地表温度比1850-1900年升高了1.1°C。",
      "exactQuote": "with global surface temperature reaching 1.1°C above 1850–1900 in 2011–2020",
      "blockId": "c-climate-001#block-5"
    },
    {
      "text": "全球温室气体排放持续增加。",
      "exactQuote": "Global greenhouse gas emissions have continued to increase",
      "blockId": "c-climate-001#block-5"
    },
    {
      "text": "历史排放和当前排放的贡献是不平等的，源于不可持续的能源使用、土地利用和土地利用变化、生活方式以及跨区域、国家内和个体间的消费和生产模式。",
      "exactQuote": "with unequal historical and ongoing contributions arising from unsustainable energy use, land use and land-use change, lifestyles and patterns of consumption and production across regions, between and within countries, and among individuals (high confidence)",
      "blockId": "c-climate-001#block-5"
    },
    {
      "text": "大气、海洋、冰冻圈和生物圈发生了广泛而迅速的变化。",
      "exactQuote": "Widespread and rapid changes in the atmosphere, ocean, cryosphere and biosphere have occurred.",
      "blockId": "c-climate-001#block-7"
    },
    {
      "text": "人类引起的气候变化已经影响到全球每个地区的许多天气和气候极端事件。",
      "exactQuote": "Human-caused climate change is already affecting many weather and climate extremes in every region across the globe.",
      "blockId": "c-climate-001#block-7"
    },
    {
      "text": "这导致了对自然和人类广泛的不利影响以及相关的损失和损害。",
      "exactQuote": "This has led to widespread adverse impacts and related losses and damages to nature and people (high confidence).",
      "blockId": "c-climate-001#block-7"
    },
    {
      "text": "历史上对当前气候变化贡献最小的脆弱社区受到了不成比例的影响。",
      "exactQuote": "Vulnerable communities who have historically contributed the least to current climate change are disproportionately affected (high confidence).",
      "blockId": "c-climate-001#block-7"
    },
    {
      "text": "自第五次评估报告以来，涉及减缓的政策和法律持续扩展。",
      "exactQuote": "Policies and laws addressing mitigation have consistently expanded since AR5.",
      "blockId": "c-climate-001#block-9"
    },
    {
      "text": "截至2021年10月宣布的国家自主贡献（NDCs）所隐含的2030年全球温室气体排放量使得21世纪升温超过1.5°C成为可能，并使限制升温低于2°C变得更加困难。",
      "exactQuote": "Global GHG emissions in 2030 implied by nationally determined contributions (NDCs) announced by October 2021 make it likely that warming will exceed 1.5°C during the 21st century and make it harder to limit warming below 2°C.",
      "blockId": "c-climate-001#block-9"
    },
    {
      "text": "已实施政策下的预计排放与国家自主贡献之间存在差距，且资金流未达到所有部门和区域实现气候目标所需的水平。",
      "exactQuote": "There are gaps between projected emissions from implemented policies and those from NDCs and finance flows fall short of the levels needed to meet climate goals across all sectors and regions. (high confidence)",
      "blockId": "c-climate-001#block-9"
    },
    {
      "text": "限制人类引起的全球变暖需要实现二氧化碳净零排放。",
      "exactQuote": "Limiting human-caused global warming requires net zero CO2 emissions.",
      "blockId": "c-climate-001#block-11"
    },
    {
      "text": "到实现二氧化碳净零排放时的累积碳排放量以及这十年温室气体减排的水平在很大程度上决定了变暖能否被限制在1.5°C或2°C。",
      "exactQuote": "Cumulative carbon emissions until the time of reaching net-zero CO2 emissions and the level of greenhouse gas emission reductions this decade largely determine whether warming can be limited to 1.5°C or 2°C (high confidence).",
      "blockId": "c-climate-001#block-11"
    },
    {
      "text": "在没有额外减排的情况下，现有化石燃料基础设施的预计二氧化碳排放量将超过1.5°C（50%概率）的剩余碳预算。",
      "exactQuote": "Projected CO2 emissions from existing fossil fuel infrastructure without additional abatement would exceed the remaining carbon budget for 1.5°C (50%) (high confidence).",
      "blockId": "c-climate-001#block-11"
    },
    {
      "text": "大约33亿至36亿人生活在高度脆弱于气候变化的环境中。",
      "exactQuote": "Approximately 3.3 to 3.6 billion people live in contexts that are highly vulnerable to climate change.",
      "blockId": "c-climate-001#block-13"
    },
    {
      "text": "人类和生态系统的脆弱性是相互依存的。",
      "exactQuote": "Human and ecosystem vulnerability are interdependent.",
      "blockId": "c-climate-001#block-13"
    },
    {
      "text": "2010年至2020年间，高度脆弱地区因洪水、干旱和风暴导致的人类死亡率比极低脆弱地区高出15倍。",
      "exactQuote": "Between 2010 and 2020, human mortality from floods, droughts and storms was 15 times higher in highly vulnerable regions, compared to regions with very low vulnerability.",
      "blockId": "c-climate-001#block-14"
    }
  ]
}
